for their thoughts and reflections. at the end

263
00:11:36,800 --> 00:11:38,000
Darren wrote back and he said:

264
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:40,080
well, I like the patrol leaders council meeting.

265
00:11:40,080 --> 00:11:41,600
during the first troop meeting night

266
00:11:41,600 --> 00:11:42,800
after a camp out

267
00:11:42,800 --> 00:11:44,240
I talked with this about it

268
00:11:44,240 --> 00:11:46,480
with our senior patrol there and scout master,

269
00:11:46,480 --> 00:11:48,160
but you still haven't told me

270
00:11:48,160 --> 00:11:49,840
what scouts who aren't involved

271
00:11:49,840 --> 00:11:52,240
with the patrol leaders council do that evening.

272
00:11:52,240 --> 00:11:54,400
I think some troops have boards of review that night,

273
00:11:54,400 --> 00:11:55,200
so it doesn't interfere

274
00:11:55,200 --> 00:11:57,200
with regular troop meetings the rest of the month.

275
00:11:57,200 --> 00:11:58,480
Well, Darren, yes,

276
00:11:58,480 --> 00:12:01,040
When the patrol leader council meets,

277
00:12:01,040 --> 00:12:03,200
okay, it's not a troop meeting at all,

278
00:12:03,200 --> 00:12:04,880
It's a patrol leaders council meeting.

279
00:12:04,880 --> 00:12:06,960
It's held the same night as a troop meeting

280
00:12:06,960 --> 00:12:09,200
after the weekend camp out.

281
00:12:09,200 --> 00:12:10,640
We do have boards of review

282
00:12:10,640 --> 00:12:11,840
and scout master conferences.

283
00:12:11,840 --> 00:12:13,920
I mean, they're available if scouts need them.

284
00:12:13,920 --> 00:12:15,040
Our troop quarter master

285
00:12:15,040 --> 00:12:16,080
will take the time to work

286
00:12:16,080 --> 00:12:18,320
with his patrol quarter masters

287
00:12:18,320 --> 00:12:19,360
to check in all the gear

288
00:12:19,360 --> 00:12:20,880
that was used during the camping trip

289
00:12:20,880 --> 00:12:21,840
on that evening.

290
00:12:21,840 --> 00:12:23,680
And scouts who aren't otherwise involved

291
00:12:23,680 --> 00:12:24,800
with any of those activities

292
00:12:24,800 --> 00:12:26,080
don't show up on that night.

293
00:12:26,320 --> 00:12:28,240
They just don't come to that meeting.

294
00:12:28,800 --> 00:12:29,840
Now I think the idea

295
00:12:29,840 --> 00:12:31,440
that older scouts could catch up

296
00:12:31,440 --> 00:12:33,360
on advancement where the younger scouts

297
00:12:33,360 --> 00:12:35,440
has some merit, okay,

298
00:12:35,440 --> 00:12:38,480
It's not a bad idea objectively.

299
00:12:38,480 --> 00:12:40,240
but it begs a number of questions

300
00:12:40,240 --> 00:12:41,280
that the scout master

301
00:12:41,280 --> 00:12:43,680
can ask the patrol leaders council,

302
00:12:43,680 --> 00:12:46,880
And this furthers what I'm trying to communicate,

303
00:12:46,880 --> 00:12:50,560
which is process rather than procedurally oriented.

304
00:12:50,560 --> 00:12:52,560
So what would the scout master ask

305
00:12:52,560 --> 00:12:54,320
if the patrol leaders council suggested,

306
00:12:54,400 --> 00:12:56,080
hey, let's have all the scouts come

307
00:12:56,080 --> 00:12:57,360
and work on advancement

308
00:12:57,360 --> 00:12:58,640
with the older scouts?

309
00:12:58,640 --> 00:13:00,000
Well, what I would ask is:

310
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:01,680
if the older scouts are there

311
00:13:01,680 --> 00:13:02,640
to help younger scouts,

312
00:13:02,640 --> 00:13:04,560
what are they working on specifically

313
00:13:04,560 --> 00:13:06,240
And who plans and decides

314
00:13:06,240 --> 00:13:07,280
what they'll be doing?

315
00:13:07,280 --> 00:13:09,280
And not only who plans and decides that,

316
00:13:09,280 --> 00:13:10,800
but how will they be planning

317
00:13:10,800 --> 00:13:12,240
and carrying out that aspect

318
00:13:12,240 --> 00:13:14,160
of that particular night?

319
00:13:14,160 --> 00:13:15,760
Do the older scouts have a current

320
00:13:15,760 --> 00:13:17,840
position of responsibility at all?

321
00:13:17,840 --> 00:13:19,680
Do they need one to advance?

322
00:13:19,680 --> 00:13:20,880
Are they going to be asked

323
00:13:20,880 --> 00:13:23,680
or assigned to carry out this idea?

324
00:13:24,640 --> 00:13:25,920
Has anybody asked them

325
00:13:25,920 --> 00:13:27,200
if they even want to do it?

326
00:13:27,200 --> 00:13:28,720
And what happens if we just have

327
00:13:28,720 --> 00:13:29,680
a general invitation,

328
00:13:29,680 --> 00:13:30,640
all the scouts show up

329
00:13:30,640 --> 00:13:32,720
and a few of them have no advancement

330
00:13:32,720 --> 00:13:33,760
to catch up on?

331
00:13:33,760 --> 00:13:35,920
And why are we doing advancement

332
00:13:35,920 --> 00:13:37,520
in a separate thing like this

333
00:13:37,520 --> 00:13:39,440
instead of as part of our regular program?

334
00:13:40,080 --> 00:13:41,600
Does that mean that we need to

335
00:13:41,600 --> 00:13:42,800
be paying more attention

336
00:13:42,800 --> 00:13:44,880
to advancement in the regular program,

337
00:13:44,880 --> 00:13:47,440
Or are we already adequately addressing that?

338
00:13:47,440 --> 00:13:49,120
So that's a lot of questions

339
00:13:49,120 --> 00:13:50,800
And I can tell you what we do in our troop.

340
00:13:50,800 --> 00:13:52,000
but the point isn't really

341
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:53,120
how we do things,

342
00:13:53,120 --> 00:13:55,600
but why we ended up doing them right

343
00:13:55,600 --> 00:13:58,240
And the engagement of the youth leadership

344
00:13:58,240 --> 00:14:00,160
in making those things happen.

345
00:14:00,160 --> 00:14:01,600
So that list of questions

346
00:14:01,600 --> 00:14:02,480
that I would ask,

347
00:14:02,480 --> 00:14:03,680
if the senior patrol leader

348
00:14:03,680 --> 00:14:05,680
suggested this as an idea.

349
00:14:05,680 --> 00:14:06,960
we'll have some answers

350
00:14:06,960 --> 00:14:08,800
and those answers will provide me

351
00:14:08,800 --> 00:14:10,720
with the opportunity to ask more questions,

352
00:14:10,720 --> 00:14:13,200
And it's really kind of an endless cycle

353
00:14:13,200 --> 00:14:14,400
of questions and answers,

354
00:14:14,400 --> 00:14:15,440
and then more questions

355
00:14:15,440 --> 00:14:16,640
and more answers

356
00:14:16,640 --> 00:14:19,280
until they go through that process

357
00:14:19,280 --> 00:14:20,800
and they begin to develop an idea

358
00:14:20,800 --> 00:14:22,640
of how they're going to accomplish

359
00:14:22,640 --> 00:14:24,560
whatever it is that we're talking about.

360
00:14:24,560 --> 00:14:27,920
So we aren't looking for the answer right

361
00:14:27,920 --> 00:14:29,840
In a set of procedures or policies

362
00:14:29,840 --> 00:14:31,520
or practices that we can adopt

363
00:14:31,520 --> 00:14:32,880
that somebody else did.

364
00:14:32,880 --> 00:14:34,319
What we're looking for

365
00:14:34,319 --> 00:14:36,400
is engaging our scouts

366
00:14:36,400 --> 00:14:40,080
in a process of finding their answers,

367
00:14:40,080 --> 00:14:41,520
And if that answer turned out

368
00:14:41,520 --> 00:14:43,439
to look exactly like what I do,

369
00:14:43,439 --> 00:14:44,080
well, you know,

370
00:14:44,800 --> 00:14:46,720
maybe that means that I'm very smart

371
00:14:47,920 --> 00:14:49,439
or just that you know,

372
00:14:49,439 --> 00:14:50,640
we had a case

373
00:14:50,640 --> 00:14:51,680
where people arrived

374
00:14:51,680 --> 00:14:52,880
at the same conclusions.

375
00:14:53,600 --> 00:14:55,200
The process involved

376
00:14:56,080 --> 00:14:58,160
in arriving at our decisions

377
00:14:58,160 --> 00:15:00,080
with the patrol leaders council

378
00:15:00,080 --> 00:15:02,720
is really more important

379
00:15:02,720 --> 00:15:04,720
than the decisions themselves,

380
00:15:04,720 --> 00:15:05,680
because procedures

381
00:15:05,680 --> 00:15:07,760
and practices and policies-

382
00:15:07,760 --> 00:15:08,880
they change all the time

383
00:15:09,440 --> 00:15:11,520
and they really aren't all that important.

384
00:15:11,520 --> 00:15:14,320
The process of how you develop

385
00:15:14,320 --> 00:15:16,080
a practice or a procedure

386
00:15:16,080 --> 00:15:17,840
is where all of the growth

387
00:15:17,840 --> 00:15:20,400
and development happens for our scouts

388
00:15:20,480 --> 00:15:22,079
and the aim of our work.

389
00:15:22,079 --> 00:15:23,920
So Darren asked me

390
00:15:23,920 --> 00:15:25,840
a pretty simple question:

391
00:15:25,840 --> 00:15:26,959
How do you run these meetings.

392
00:15:26,959 --> 00:15:28,720
Okay, my answer was:

393
00:15:28,720 --> 00:15:30,640
well, it's not really important

394
00:15:30,640 --> 00:15:32,079
about how I run these meetings.

395
00:15:32,079 --> 00:15:33,600
What's important is

396
00:15:33,600 --> 00:15:35,360
the basic logic behind

397
00:15:35,360 --> 00:15:36,800
what we're up to right,

398
00:15:36,800 --> 00:15:37,680
Which is

399
00:15:37,680 --> 00:15:38,959
scouts join scouting

400
00:15:38,959 --> 00:15:40,480
to do the things that scouts do,

401
00:15:41,040 --> 00:15:42,240
which is to go camping

402
00:15:42,240 --> 00:15:43,280
with their buddies.

403
00:15:43,280 --> 00:15:44,240
and when they go camping

404
00:15:44,240 --> 00:15:44,800
with their buddies,

405
00:15:44,800 --> 00:15:46,079
they got to do all this stuff.

406
00:15:46,079 --> 00:15:47,439
They have to build fires

407
00:15:47,439 --> 00:15:48,640
and set up tents

408
00:15:48,640 --> 00:15:50,000
and decide on campsites,

409
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:51,440
and what does that sound like?

410
00:15:51,440 --> 00:15:53,680
Well, those are advancement requirements, right?

411
00:15:53,680 --> 00:15:54,800
So we're doing those

412
00:15:54,800 --> 00:15:55,840
in the natural course

413
00:15:55,840 --> 00:15:57,600
of the activities that we're pursuing,

414
00:15:57,600 --> 00:15:59,440
and so it kind of begs the question for me:

415
00:15:59,440 --> 00:16:00,400
why do you have to have

416
00:16:00,400 --> 00:16:01,920
a separate time for advancement?

417
00:16:01,920 --> 00:16:04,080
This should be happening right

418
00:16:04,080 --> 00:16:05,680
As we're doing things,

419
00:16:05,680 --> 00:16:07,440
and I can understand

420
00:16:07,440 --> 00:16:08,720
having some time set aside-

421
00:16:08,720 --> 00:16:10,320
especially if it's a larger troop-

422
00:16:10,320 --> 00:16:12,160
for older scouts to sit down

423
00:16:12,160 --> 00:16:14,560
and to sign requirements off

424
00:16:14,560 --> 00:16:15,600
for younger scouts

425
00:16:15,600 --> 00:16:16,560
or something like that.

426
00:16:17,280 --> 00:16:18,640
But again, you know,

427
00:16:18,640 --> 00:16:19,600
my question would be:

428
00:16:19,600 --> 00:16:20,880
well, why isn't this happening

429
00:16:20,880 --> 00:16:22,160
just in the natural course

430
00:16:22,160 --> 00:16:23,200
of what we're doing?

431
00:16:23,200 --> 00:16:25,200
But I repeat myself again,

432
00:16:25,200 --> 00:16:26,560
the most important thing

433
00:16:26,560 --> 00:16:28,560
is engaging our youth leadership

434
00:16:28,560 --> 00:16:30,080
in this process

435
00:16:30,080 --> 00:16:32,720
of looking at the basic logic of scouting,

436
00:16:32,720 --> 00:16:34,400
answering a lot of questions

437
00:16:34,400 --> 00:16:35,680
and to beginning to develop

438
00:16:35,680 --> 00:16:37,200
their own resolutions

439
00:16:37,200 --> 00:16:39,120
and answers and procedures

440
00:16:39,120 --> 00:16:40,320
and practices,

441
00:16:40,320 --> 00:16:41,760
because that's really

442
00:16:41,760 --> 00:16:43,120
the work that we're aimed at.

443
00:16:43,840 --> 00:16:45,200
That's really what develops

444
00:16:45,200 --> 00:16:46,560
character and leadership

445
00:16:46,560 --> 00:16:48,560
and responsibility in our scouts.

446
00:16:48,560 --> 00:16:50,240
So I hope that's not too confusing.

447
00:16:51,040 --> 00:16:53,040
Scouting is not easy to get sometimes,

448
00:16:53,040 --> 00:16:54,320
because it's all about

449
00:16:54,320 --> 00:16:56,400
what we're really aimed at

450
00:16:56,400 --> 00:16:58,000
and not necessarily

451
00:16:58,000 --> 00:16:59,520
the practices and procedures

452
00:16:59,520 --> 00:17:00,720
we use to get there.

453
00:17:00,720 --> 00:17:02,400
Once you understand the aim,

454
00:17:02,400 --> 00:17:03,280
once you understand

455
00:17:03,280 --> 00:17:04,560
what's really important,

456
00:17:04,560 --> 00:17:06,080
then all the other pieces

457
00:17:06,080 --> 00:17:07,680
fall into place pretty naturally.

458
00:17:08,480 --> 00:17:09,680
I heard from Ty Williams

459
00:17:09,680 --> 00:17:12,880
in Clarkston, Washington. Clarkston-

460
00:17:12,880 --> 00:17:14,720
What a lovely name for a town,

461
00:17:14,720 --> 00:17:15,760
Wouldn't you say? huh.

462
00:17:16,320 --> 00:17:17,520
Anyway, Ty wrote in

463
00:17:17,520 --> 00:17:18,480
to ask me this question.

464
00:17:18,480 --> 00:17:19,920
He says I'm going to be scout master

465
00:17:19,920 --> 00:17:21,119
for a young troop

466
00:17:21,119 --> 00:17:22,160
and really we're working

467
00:17:22,160 --> 00:17:23,359
with the charter organization

468
00:17:23,359 --> 00:17:24,240
to get the troop up

469
00:17:24,240 --> 00:17:24,960
and running again.

470
00:17:24,960 --> 00:17:26,720
It's been dormant for a while.

471
00:17:26,720 --> 00:17:28,160
We'll have six youth

472
00:17:28,160 --> 00:17:29,520
when the charter is signed.

473
00:17:30,080 --> 00:17:30,879
Five of them

474
00:17:30,879 --> 00:17:33,120
will be Weebelow's crossovers.

475
00:17:33,120 --> 00:17:35,120
So how do we adult volunteers

476
00:17:35,120 --> 00:17:36,080
guide these youth

477
00:17:36,080 --> 00:17:37,520
in the patrol method

478
00:17:37,520 --> 00:17:38,879
when they're so young?

479
00:17:38,879 --> 00:17:40,320
I do have one scout

480
00:17:40,320 --> 00:17:41,600
that is 17

481
00:17:41,600 --> 00:17:43,040
who's volunteered to participate

482
00:17:43,040 --> 00:17:43,680
with the troop

483
00:17:43,680 --> 00:17:44,960
as a senior scout

484
00:17:44,960 --> 00:17:45,760
and help out.

485
00:17:45,760 --> 00:17:46,560
Well, Ty, it sounds

486
00:17:46,560 --> 00:17:47,919
like you have a great thing going

487
00:17:47,919 --> 00:17:49,280
and it may seem small

488
00:17:49,280 --> 00:17:50,639
and the scouts may seem young.

489
00:17:50,639 --> 00:17:52,080
but these are not barriers,

490
00:17:52,080 --> 00:17:53,520
These are your strengths.

491
00:17:53,520 --> 00:17:54,320
Okay,

492
00:17:54,320 --> 00:17:55,440
And you're going to give them

493
00:17:55,440 --> 00:17:56,560
a wonderful experience

494
00:17:56,560 --> 00:17:58,000
because with that many guys,

495
00:17:58,560 --> 00:17:59,679
you have a patrol,

496
00:17:59,679 --> 00:18:00,639
So there's no need

497
00:18:00,639 --> 00:18:01,679
for a senior patrol leader

498
00:18:01,679 --> 00:18:02,720
or patrol leaders council

499
00:18:02,720 --> 00:18:03,520
or anything like that.

500
00:18:03,520 --> 00:18:04,560
Don't get distracted

501
00:18:04,560 --> 00:18:05,600
by those things.

502
00:18:05,600 --> 00:18:06,800
If I was in your shoes,

503
00:18:06,800 --> 00:18:07,520
what I would do

504
00:18:07,520 --> 00:18:08,320
is I would sit down

505
00:18:08,320 --> 00:18:09,679
with that older scout

506
00:18:09,679 --> 00:18:10,800
and tell him

507
00:18:10,800 --> 00:18:11,440
he's going to be

508
00:18:11,440 --> 00:18:12,080
the patrol leader

509
00:18:12,080 --> 00:18:13,280
for the next three months

510
00:18:13,280 --> 00:18:15,440
and that he has these three goals.

511
00:18:15,440 --> 00:18:16,080
The first is

512
00:18:16,080 --> 00:18:17,280
to plan and execute

513
00:18:17,280 --> 00:18:19,040
three monthly activities,

514
00:18:19,040 --> 00:18:20,000
with at least two of them

515
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:21,520
being camping overnight.

516
00:18:21,520 --> 00:18:22,560
you know, accepting

517
00:18:22,560 --> 00:18:23,520
that you're getting up

518
00:18:23,520 --> 00:18:24,240
and getting moving

519
00:18:24,240 --> 00:18:25,199
and getting rolling,

520
00:18:25,199 --> 00:18:26,639
I think getting two campouts

521
00:18:26,639 --> 00:18:27,679
in in the next three or four

522
00:18:27,679 --> 00:18:29,840
months is a pretty good goal.

523
00:18:30,399 --> 00:18:31,679
So to prepare

524
00:18:31,679 --> 00:18:32,639
for those activities,

525
00:18:32,639 --> 00:18:33,840
he'll need to do some planning

526
00:18:33,840 --> 00:18:34,480
right

527
00:18:34,480 --> 00:18:35,760
And he'll need to plan

528
00:18:35,760 --> 00:18:37,199
the patrol meetings

529
00:18:37,199 --> 00:18:37,919
that you're going to have

530
00:18:37,919 --> 00:18:38,879
every week

531
00:18:38,879 --> 00:18:39,520
to train

532
00:18:39,520 --> 00:18:41,040
and prepare his scouts

533
00:18:41,040 --> 00:18:41,840
to go camping

534
00:18:41,840 --> 00:18:43,679
and to do whatever they've planned.

535
00:18:43,679 --> 00:18:45,199
So the second goal

536
00:18:45,280 --> 00:18:46,480
is, in three months' time

537
00:18:46,480 --> 00:18:48,560
he'll have trained all of his scouts

538
00:18:48,560 --> 00:18:49,840
to take over

539
00:18:49,840 --> 00:18:51,600
his job as patrol leader

540
00:18:51,600 --> 00:18:53,040
and they'll have an election

541
00:18:53,040 --> 00:18:53,680
and they'll choose

542
00:18:53,680 --> 00:18:55,120
the next patrol leader.

543
00:18:55,120 --> 00:18:56,560
And the third goal

544
00:18:56,560 --> 00:18:57,520
is that

545
00:18:57,520 --> 00:18:59,520
he'll get all his scouts

546
00:18:59,520 --> 00:19:00,480
to advance

547
00:19:00,480 --> 00:19:02,000
at least one rank

548
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:03,600
in those three months.

549
00:19:03,600 --> 00:19:04,800
Now, from there,

550
00:19:04,800 --> 00:19:06,480
you can open up a conversation

551
00:19:06,480 --> 00:19:07,600
that's going to go on

552
00:19:07,600 --> 00:19:09,600
while he's the patrol leader, right,

553
00:19:09,600 --> 00:19:10,800
He can start telling you

554
00:19:10,800 --> 00:19:12,320
what he'll need from you.

555
00:19:12,320 --> 00:19:13,200
You'll make it a point

556
00:19:13,200 --> 00:19:13,840
to discuss

557
00:19:13,840 --> 00:19:15,600
how things are going often

558
00:19:15,600 --> 00:19:16,320
and you'll be there

559
00:19:16,320 --> 00:19:18,000
if he has any questions.

560
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:20,399
But you'll begin asking questions.

561
00:19:20,399 --> 00:19:21,199
So how are you going to make

562
00:19:21,199 --> 00:19:21,919
these goals work?

563
00:19:21,919 --> 00:19:23,360
What are your three monthly activities?

564
00:19:23,360 --> 00:19:25,120
What do your meeting plans look like?

565
00:19:25,120 --> 00:19:26,000
Do you need help

566
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:27,040
putting those together?

567
00:19:27,040 --> 00:19:28,959
How are your scouts doing on advancement?

568
00:19:28,959 --> 00:19:30,560
What do you need to do with them?

569
00:19:30,560 --> 00:19:32,240
Is that part of your activity plan?

570
00:19:32,240 --> 00:19:33,520
Is that part of your meeting plan?

571
00:19:33,520 --> 00:19:34,800
How are you going to get all these guys

572
00:19:34,800 --> 00:19:35,520
to scout rank

573
00:19:35,520 --> 00:19:36,399
or to tender foot

574
00:19:36,399 --> 00:19:38,000
within this next three months?

575
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:39,439
So it sounds like a big challenge

576
00:19:39,439 --> 00:19:40,159
and it is,

577
00:19:40,159 --> 00:19:41,679
but keep an open dialogue

578
00:19:41,679 --> 00:19:42,800
and you're going to be amazed

579
00:19:42,800 --> 00:19:43,679
at how things go.

580
00:19:43,760 --> 00:19:45,200
If you have an older scout

581
00:19:45,200 --> 00:19:46,960
who's really interested in doing this-

582
00:19:46,960 --> 00:19:48,160
and having that amount of

583
00:19:48,160 --> 00:19:49,280
responsibility

584
00:19:49,280 --> 00:19:50,560
seems to motivate him-

585
00:19:50,560 --> 00:19:51,680
you're good to go

586
00:19:51,680 --> 00:19:53,040
and I'll be really interested

587
00:19:53,040 --> 00:19:54,240
to hear how things happen.

588
00:19:54,960 --> 00:19:56,320
Here's an anonymous question:

589
00:19:57,120 --> 00:19:59,360
Is there an official BSA policy

590
00:19:59,360 --> 00:20:01,120
on asking registered adults

591
00:20:01,120 --> 00:20:02,160
to leave the troop.

592
00:20:02,960 --> 00:20:04,400
Hmm, we have a pair of parents

593
00:20:04,400 --> 00:20:05,680
who continue to attend

594
00:20:05,680 --> 00:20:06,240
troop meetings

595
00:20:06,240 --> 00:20:07,120
and committee meetings

596
00:20:07,120 --> 00:20:09,120
after their sons have moved on,

597
00:20:09,120 --> 00:20:10,880
They've graduated from high school

598
00:20:10,880 --> 00:20:12,400
and they've gone on to college,

599
00:20:12,400 --> 00:20:13,680
and neither of these people

600
00:20:13,680 --> 00:20:15,440
have any position in the troop

601
00:20:15,440 --> 00:20:17,280
and they intend to be disruptive

602
00:20:17,280 --> 00:20:18,560
and divisive and difficult.

603
00:20:19,120 --> 00:20:20,640
How do we get them out of our hair?

604
00:20:21,200 --> 00:20:24,240
Well, there's no official policy

605
00:20:24,240 --> 00:20:26,000
or procedure I've ever found

606
00:20:26,640 --> 00:20:28,800
that outlines exactly how to do this.

607
00:20:28,800 --> 00:20:30,720
It's a pretty simple thing to do, though.

608
00:20:30,720 --> 00:20:32,160
Now I will say this:

609
00:20:32,160 --> 00:20:33,360
it's a pretty rare thing

610
00:20:33,360 --> 00:20:34,720
that we need to ask somebody

611
00:20:34,720 --> 00:20:35,520
to step away

612
00:20:35,520 --> 00:20:36,800
from a volunteer position,

613
00:20:37,440 --> 00:20:39,120
but these folks don't have a position.

614
00:20:39,120 --> 00:20:40,240
I guess they're just staying

615
00:20:40,240 --> 00:20:41,440
registered with the troop

616
00:20:41,440 --> 00:20:43,040
for one reason or another.

617
00:20:43,040 --> 00:20:44,480
but if they're being disruptive

618
00:20:44,480 --> 00:20:45,280
and difficult,

619
00:20:45,280 --> 00:20:46,800
you can try and play nice

620
00:20:46,800 --> 00:20:48,160
and you can try and talk to them

621
00:20:48,160 --> 00:20:50,400
and you can try to resolve things,

622
00:20:50,400 --> 00:20:52,880
but sometimes that just doesn't work.

623
00:20:52,880 --> 00:20:54,080
so what do you do next?

624
00:20:54,080 --> 00:20:56,400
Well, the chartered organization

625
00:20:56,400 --> 00:20:57,840
representative and the committee

626
00:20:57,840 --> 00:20:59,600
chairman put their heads together

627
00:20:59,600 --> 00:21:01,040
and they send a letter-

628
00:21:01,040 --> 00:21:04,240
and this is a real paper snail mail

629
00:21:04,240 --> 00:21:06,160
letter in an envelope, right,

630
00:21:06,160 --> 00:21:08,000
And they can hand deliver a copy.

631
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:09,280
they can put it in the mail

632
00:21:09,280 --> 00:21:10,960
however they want to handle it.

633
00:21:10,960 --> 00:21:12,240
but it's a real letter,

634
00:21:12,240 --> 00:21:12,960
not an email,

635
00:21:12,960 --> 00:21:14,800
and I'll talk about that in a second.

636
00:21:14,800 --> 00:21:17,280
So the letter states very clearly

637
00:21:17,280 --> 00:21:19,040
that these folks are not allowed

638
00:21:19,040 --> 00:21:20,560
to attend meetings, committee meetings

639
00:21:20,560 --> 00:21:21,920
or any function of the unit,

640
00:21:21,920 --> 00:21:22,960
and in this letter

641
00:21:22,960 --> 00:21:24,640
you don't have to state causes.

642
00:21:24,640 --> 00:21:26,880
this is not like firing an employee

643
00:21:26,880 --> 00:21:29,120
or you're telling a volunteer

644
00:21:29,120 --> 00:21:31,040
that their involvement

645
00:21:31,040 --> 00:21:32,960
is no longer necessary.

646
00:21:32,960 --> 00:21:34,080
So let me give you an idea

647
00:21:34,080 --> 00:21:36,000
of what I would put in a letter like that.

648
00:21:36,000 --> 00:21:37,440
it would be: you know,

649
00:21:37,440 --> 00:21:38,640
Dear Mr and Mrs X,

650
00:21:38,640 --> 00:21:40,640
as representative of the chartering organization

651
00:21:40,720 --> 00:21:41,680
of our troop,

652
00:21:41,680 --> 00:21:43,440
this letter serves as notification

653
00:21:43,440 --> 00:21:44,640
that you are not to attend

654
00:21:44,640 --> 00:21:46,800
any function or meetings of the troop

655
00:21:46,800 --> 00:21:48,080
in any capacity.

656
00:21:48,080 --> 00:21:49,120
I'm taking this action

657
00:21:49,120 --> 00:21:50,960
on behalf of our chartering organization

658
00:21:50,960 --> 00:21:52,080
after receiving complaints

659
00:21:52,080 --> 00:21:53,200
about undue interference

660
00:21:53,200 --> 00:21:54,960
with the troops volunteers.

661
00:21:54,960 --> 00:21:56,080
this decision is final.

662
00:21:56,080 --> 00:21:58,000
there will be no further discussion.

663
00:21:58,000 --> 00:22:00,880
Now that all sounds really harsh and mean,

664
00:22:00,880 --> 00:22:02,640
but if you've worked to try

665
00:22:02,640 --> 00:22:03,680
and resolve this

666
00:22:03,680 --> 00:22:05,840
and they're not working along with you,

667
00:22:05,840 --> 00:22:07,440
they're not really going to take a hint.

668
00:22:07,440 --> 00:22:08,640
you have to spell this out

669
00:22:08,640 --> 00:22:09,600
pretty carefully

670
00:22:09,600 --> 00:22:11,040
and it's almost certain

671
00:22:11,040 --> 00:22:12,960
you aren't going to win them over with kindness.

672
00:22:12,960 --> 00:22:14,160
I want to reiterate:

673
00:22:14,160 --> 00:22:15,600
don't email this notice,

674
00:22:15,600 --> 00:22:17,040
because email

675
00:22:17,040 --> 00:22:18,560
takes on a life of its own.

676
00:22:18,560 --> 00:22:19,840
the best course

677
00:22:19,840 --> 00:22:21,520
is to either mail

678
00:22:21,520 --> 00:22:22,080
the letter

679
00:22:22,080 --> 00:22:23,200
or hand deliver it,

680
00:22:23,200 --> 00:22:24,160
and hand delivery,

681
00:22:24,160 --> 00:22:25,680
I think, would probably be the option

682
00:22:25,680 --> 00:22:26,640
that I would take

683
00:22:26,640 --> 00:22:28,240
now. there'll likely be a reaction,

684
00:22:28,240 --> 00:22:29,840
and it may be a very ugly reaction,

685
00:22:29,840 --> 00:22:31,200
but there is no recourse

686
00:22:31,200 --> 00:22:32,080
through the council

687
00:22:32,080 --> 00:22:33,200
or the district

688
00:22:33,200 --> 00:22:34,960
because charter organizations

689
00:22:34,960 --> 00:22:36,720
have the absolute authority

690
00:22:36,720 --> 00:22:38,240
to choose who volunteers

691
00:22:38,240 --> 00:22:40,400
and to fire volunteers at any time,

692
00:22:40,400 --> 00:22:42,240
for cause or no cause at all.

693
00:22:42,240 --> 00:22:43,440
Now your scout executive

694
00:22:43,440 --> 00:22:44,880
and your district executive

695
00:22:44,880 --> 00:22:46,640
would probably appreciate a copy of the letter,

696
00:22:46,640 --> 00:22:48,720
but you don't really need their approval or permission

697
00:22:49,440 --> 00:22:50,720
as long as you have

698
00:22:50,720 --> 00:22:52,080
the permission and approval

699
00:22:52,080 --> 00:22:54,080
of the charter organization

700
00:22:54,080 --> 00:22:55,760
to take this course of action.

701
00:22:55,760 --> 00:22:57,760
nobody likes situations like this.

702
00:22:57,760 --> 00:22:59,280
they come up from time to time.

703
00:22:59,280 --> 00:23:01,040
thankfully, they're not very common,

704
00:23:01,040 --> 00:23:02,480
and because they're so uncommon,

705
00:23:02,480 --> 00:23:05,840
we sometimes aren't quite sure what to do,

706
00:23:05,840 --> 00:23:07,440
and I offer my advice.

707
00:23:07,440 --> 00:23:08,800
I have never been able to find

708
00:23:08,800 --> 00:23:10,640
a specific policy statement

709
00:23:10,640 --> 00:23:11,440
or procedure

710
00:23:11,440 --> 00:23:13,840
about how to get rid of a volunteer,

711
00:23:13,840 --> 00:23:15,280
and my advice is premised

712
00:23:15,280 --> 00:23:16,480
on the assumption that

713
00:23:16,480 --> 00:23:17,760
you've already talked this around

714
00:23:17,760 --> 00:23:19,760
and you tried to resolve this with them

715
00:23:19,760 --> 00:23:21,120
and it just ain't gonna work

716
00:23:21,120 --> 00:23:22,000
okay.

717
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:24,400
so if you know of policies or procedures

718
00:23:24,400 --> 00:23:26,000
that do affect this

719
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:28,000
and would shed some light on the question.

720
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:29,840
please do get in touch with me.

721
00:23:29,840 --> 00:23:31,520
while we're talking about difficult stuff,

722
00:23:32,080 --> 00:23:33,440
here's an email that came to me

723
00:23:33,440 --> 00:23:34,960
from a youth member

724
00:23:34,960 --> 00:23:37,200
and I'll mention very quickly.

725
00:23:37,200 --> 00:23:38,800
I'm happy to receive communication

726
00:23:38,800 --> 00:23:39,760
from youth members.

727
00:23:39,760 --> 00:23:41,280
I always tell them

728
00:23:41,280 --> 00:23:43,200
to please include a parent

729
00:23:43,200 --> 00:23:45,520
in any future emails.

730
00:23:45,520 --> 00:23:47,360
I follow the BSA policy

731
00:23:47,360 --> 00:23:49,360
of always making sure there's somebody else-

732
00:23:49,360 --> 00:23:52,000
and preferably that's the child's parent-

733
00:23:52,000 --> 00:23:53,840
is a party to the conversation

734
00:23:53,840 --> 00:23:55,120
I'm gonna have via email

735
00:23:55,120 --> 00:23:56,480
with a youth member.

736
00:23:56,480 --> 00:23:58,720
but anyway, let's get back to this question.

737
00:23:58,720 --> 00:24:00,080
we have a scout in our troop

738
00:24:00,080 --> 00:24:02,800
who has probably some mental health issues

739
00:24:02,800 --> 00:24:04,560
and he's usually a very good scout,

740
00:24:04,560 --> 00:24:06,400
but sometimes he'll kind of go off

741
00:24:06,400 --> 00:24:08,480
on either me or my father,

742
00:24:08,480 --> 00:24:09,600
the scout master.

743
00:24:09,600 --> 00:24:11,280
we have a true policy that I've written

744
00:24:11,280 --> 00:24:13,200
and submitted to the patrol leaders council,

745
00:24:13,200 --> 00:24:14,640
as I am a patrol leader.

746
00:24:14,640 --> 00:24:16,960
this policy has discussed behavioral issues

747
00:24:16,960 --> 00:24:19,680
such as scouts breaking the scout oath and law.

748
00:24:19,680 --> 00:24:23,520
I sure do not hope that we will have to ask this scout to leave,

749
00:24:23,520 --> 00:24:26,400
but I also don't want him to physically harm anybody.

750
00:24:26,960 --> 00:24:28,400
you really don't need a policy

751
00:24:28,400 --> 00:24:29,200
or a set of rules

752
00:24:29,200 --> 00:24:30,640
because you already have them

753
00:24:30,640 --> 00:24:32,880
and this is the scout oath and law.

754
00:24:32,880 --> 00:24:34,000
you do not want

755
00:24:34,000 --> 00:24:35,200
or need anything else,

756
00:24:35,200 --> 00:24:37,360
and I'll explain why. in my answer,

757
00:24:37,360 --> 00:24:39,760
I also want to make sure that it's understood

758
00:24:39,760 --> 00:24:41,440
that I do not think

759
00:24:41,440 --> 00:24:43,200
it is a good idea for youth leaders

760
00:24:43,200 --> 00:24:46,160
to try and manage difficult behavior on their own.

761
00:24:46,160 --> 00:24:48,160
this is why adults volunteer for scouting

762
00:24:48,160 --> 00:24:50,160
to help you handle these types of things.

763
00:24:50,160 --> 00:24:52,000
this is one for the adults.

764
00:24:52,000 --> 00:24:52,880
okay,

765
00:24:52,880 --> 00:24:55,360
so let's just talk about misbehavior in general.

766
00:24:55,920 --> 00:24:57,520
scout misbehaves

767
00:24:57,520 --> 00:24:58,880
causes a problem.

768
00:24:58,880 --> 00:25:00,160
the next step is:

769
00:25:00,160 --> 00:25:02,720
is he's going to sit down and talk to the scout master?

770
00:25:02,720 --> 00:25:05,040
the scout master is going to discuss this with him

771
00:25:05,040 --> 00:25:06,800
and hopefully arrive at a resolution,

772
00:25:06,800 --> 00:25:08,240
and that's what will happen

773
00:25:08,240 --> 00:25:09,680
nine out of ten times.

774
00:25:09,680 --> 00:25:10,960
maybe somebody got angry,

775
00:25:10,960 --> 00:25:12,320
maybe somebody got out of line

776
00:25:12,320 --> 00:25:13,600
or went off, like you said,

777
00:25:14,240 --> 00:25:16,080
and they need to make some apologies,

778
00:25:16,080 --> 00:25:16,960
patch things up,

779
00:25:16,960 --> 00:25:19,120
and it's very easy to do that way.

780
00:25:19,120 --> 00:25:20,560
I want to add right here

781
00:25:20,560 --> 00:25:22,320
for the adult scouters who are listening in:

782
00:25:22,320 --> 00:25:23,200
let's remember,

783
00:25:23,200 --> 00:25:24,080
as scouters

784
00:25:24,080 --> 00:25:26,480
we don't ever use corrective punishment.

785
00:25:26,480 --> 00:25:29,520
sometimes there's proportionate consequences to an action.

786
00:25:29,520 --> 00:25:30,720
if they made a mess

787
00:25:30,720 --> 00:25:31,920
or they broke something,

788
00:25:31,920 --> 00:25:33,360
they have to clean up the mess

789
00:25:33,360 --> 00:25:34,240
or fix something.

790
00:25:34,240 --> 00:25:35,920
maybe they have to apologize to somebody.

791
00:25:35,920 --> 00:25:37,280
but we never use punishment

792
00:25:37,280 --> 00:25:40,720
and we especially never allow our youth leaders

793
00:25:40,720 --> 00:25:43,120
to use any kind of punishment whatsoever.

794
00:25:43,120 --> 00:25:44,640
we do not punish.

795
00:25:44,640 --> 00:25:46,560
that is a parent's job.

796
00:25:46,560 --> 00:25:47,920
back to what I was saying:

797
00:25:47,920 --> 00:25:49,760
if there is an instance of misbehavior,

798
00:25:49,760 --> 00:25:50,880
the scout's going to sit down

799
00:25:50,880 --> 00:25:52,080
and talk to the scout master.

800
00:25:52,080 --> 00:25:53,680
and exactly what happens

801
00:25:53,680 --> 00:25:55,520
when the scout master talks to the scout

802
00:25:55,520 --> 00:25:58,000
is not something I can absolutely define for you,

803
00:25:58,000 --> 00:26:00,800
because every instance of bad behavior

804
00:26:00,800 --> 00:26:02,400
needs to be addressed on its own.

805
00:26:02,400 --> 00:26:03,280
every person

806
00:26:03,280 --> 00:26:06,080
and every interaction they have with other people

807
00:26:06,080 --> 00:26:08,560
it's going to be different in one way or another,

808
00:26:08,560 --> 00:26:10,000
and that's why you don't want

809
00:26:10,000 --> 00:26:12,320
specific policies, procedures and rules

810
00:26:12,320 --> 00:26:14,320
to be written about things like this,

811
00:26:14,320 --> 00:26:15,680
because you have to deal with these

812
00:26:15,680 --> 00:26:17,520
on an individual basis.

813
00:26:17,520 --> 00:26:19,760
so there's some very simple, logical things

814
00:26:19,760 --> 00:26:21,200
that happen when the scout master

815
00:26:21,200 --> 00:26:23,120
and the scout are talking to each other.

816
00:26:23,120 --> 00:26:25,920
if they can, as I said, resolve the problem

817
00:26:25,920 --> 00:26:26,880
then and there-

818
00:26:26,880 --> 00:26:28,400
and this happens most of the times

819
00:26:28,400 --> 00:26:30,480
because you know scouts are usually pretty good

820
00:26:30,480 --> 00:26:33,360
and misbehavior isn't usually all that bad-

821
00:26:33,360 --> 00:26:34,240
then we're done.

822
00:26:34,240 --> 00:26:36,160
if it's a pattern of misbehavior-

823
00:26:36,160 --> 00:26:38,160
if the same thing happens more than once,

824
00:26:38,160 --> 00:26:39,120
that's a pattern-

825
00:26:39,120 --> 00:26:42,640
then it's usually time to involve the scout's parents-

826
00:26:42,640 --> 00:26:43,600
and I say usually

827
00:26:43,600 --> 00:26:46,080
because it all depends on those individual elements

828
00:26:46,080 --> 00:26:47,120
that I was speaking about-

829
00:26:47,120 --> 00:26:48,880
and when the scout's parents get involved.

830
00:26:48,880 --> 00:26:50,560
the message to them is simple:

831
00:26:50,560 --> 00:26:52,400
your son is misbehaving

832
00:26:52,400 --> 00:26:55,680
and he can't participate in scouts until you can assure us

833
00:26:55,680 --> 00:26:57,120
corrected that misbehavior

834
00:26:57,760 --> 00:26:59,440
and he will be able to

835
00:26:59,440 --> 00:27:02,400
observe the scout oath and law while he's here with us.

836
00:27:02,400 --> 00:27:03,680
so take him home,

837
00:27:03,680 --> 00:27:04,720
work this out

838
00:27:04,720 --> 00:27:06,720
and when you're sure he can behave

839
00:27:06,720 --> 00:27:08,160
according to the scout oath and law,

840
